Optimal Solution - Dynamic programming solution to count distinct subsequences of a string forming a target string.
                   For each character in s, decide whether to use it to match t or skip it, and accumulate counts using DP.

class Solution {
    public int numDistinct(String s, String t) {
        // Lengths of source string s and target string t
        int m = s.length(), n = t.length();
        // dp[i][j] = number of distinct subsequences of
        // s[0..j-1] that form t[0..i-1]
        int[][] dp = new int[n + 1][m + 1];
        // Base case: empty target string can be formed in exactly
        // one way from any prefix of s (by deleting all characters)
        for (int j = 0; j <= m; j++) {
            dp[0][j] = 1;
        }
        // Fill DP table
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < m; j++) {
                // If characters match, we can either:
                // 1) use this character (dp[i][j])
                // 2) skip this character (dp[i+1][j])
                if (t.charAt(i) == s.charAt(j)) {
                    dp[i + 1][j + 1] = dp[i][j] + dp[i + 1][j];
                }
                // If characters don't match, we must skip s[j]
                else {
                    dp[i + 1][j + 1] = dp[i + 1][j];
                }
            }
        }
        // Final answer: ways to form full t from full s
        return dp[n][m];
    }
}

Time Complexity :- O(n * m).
Space Complexity :- O(n * m).
